= Common-token bias =
== Overview ==
'''Common-token bias''' is a proposed language-model tendency to favor output labels represented by tokens that are more common or otherwise favored by the model's learned distribution.

== Proposed mechanism ==
In few-shot classification, arbitrary label tokens can carry unequal prior probabilities independent of the intended class semantics.

== Interpretability caution ==
The label is not always a clean explanation. Controlled work has shown that effects previously attributed to common-token bias can instead arise from primacy or recency. The observed prediction pattern and its mechanism must therefore be separated.

== References ==
* Zhao et al., “Calibrate Before Use: Improving Few-Shot Performance of Language Models”, ICML 2021.
* Mina et al., “Cognitive Biases, Task Complexity, and Result Interpretability in Large Language Models”, COLING 2025.

